d was the super-heavyweight class for lifters with a bodyweight of more than 81 kg, down from the 87 kg contested in Tokyo."] "\n\n" [:p {} "A star-studied field competed in Paris, with defending Olympic champion and world record holder " [:a {:href "/athletes/141795"} "Li Wenwen"] " of China being the favorite to win gold again. Great Britian’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/143088"} "Emily Campbell"] ", who won silver in Tokyo, was present in Paris, but the previous bronze medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/126095"} "Sarah Robles"] " of the USA was not, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/155588"} "Mary Theisen-Lappen"] " qualified ahead of her. The field also featured the World champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/155570"} "Park Hye-Jeong"] " (KOR), the Pan American champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/2101616"} "Lisseth Ayoví"] " (ECU), and the South-East Asian Games champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/2102605"} "Duangaksorn Chaidee"] " (THA)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Li led the way in the snatch with 136 kg, five kilograms ahead of Park and 10 kilograms ahead of Campbell. The same pattern was repeated in the clean &amp; jerk, with Li continuing to dominate when she lifted 173 kg. This left the result in no doubt, with Li winning her second consecutive Olympic weightlifting gold, with a total of 309 kg. Park finished with 299 kg to win silver, ahead of Campbell, who lifted 288 kg."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Kilograms"] [:th {} "Bodyweight"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/141795"} "Li Wenwen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} "309"] [:td {} "149.25"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/a